<description>
Add the four colored diagonal corner markers around every grey 2x2 square.

Input structure
- The grid has black background pixels and one or more 4-connected grey
  foreground objects.
- Every grey object is a solid 2x2 square with a one-cell black margin at
  each diagonal outside corner.

Rule
- Preserve the input grid.
- For each grey square, paint blue at the northwest outside corner, red at
  the northeast outside corner, green at the southwest outside corner, and
  yellow at the southeast outside corner.

Key insight
- The grey squares are fixed anchors; the output is a local decoration of
  each square's bounding box, not a movement or matching problem.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "transform_in_place",
  "src": "solid grey 2x2 square objects on a black background",
  "transform": "preserve each grey square and paint blue, red, green, and yellow pixels at its northwest, northeast, southwest, and southeast diagonal outside corners"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 10-15 rows x 10-15 cols, always square [observed]
  background: BLACK
  objects:
    type: solid GREY 2x2 squares
    count: 1-6
    placement: each square top-left (r,c) has r in [1, H-3], c in [1, W-3]
    non-overlap: each square's 4x4 zone [r-1..r+2, c-1..c+2] must not overlap any other square's zone; equivalently for any two top-lefts, abs(dr) >= 4 OR abs(dc) >= 4
    input_colors: only BLACK and GREY
  transform:
    rule: for each GREY 2x2 at (r,c), paint four diagonal corner markers
    markers: NW=(r-1,c-1)=BLUE, NE=(r-1,c+2)=RED, SW=(r+2,c-1)=GREEN, SE=(r+2,c+2)=YELLOW
    all marker cells must be BLACK in input (guaranteed by zone non-overlap)

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct forward (transform is trivial local decoration)
  steps:
    1. pick grid size N x N, N in [10, 15]
    2. pick number of squares k in [1, 6], scaled to grid size
    3. place k grey 2x2 squares on BLACK grid using greedy random placement; for each candidate (r,c) with r in [1, N-3], c in [1, N-3], verify its 4x4 zone does not overlap any already-placed zone
    4. input is the resulting BLACK+GREY grid; output copies input then paints the four colored markers per square
```
</generation_spec>
</reference_puzzle>

